      "cooked": "<p>I opened this issue on GitHub regarding this issue:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubissue\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/frappe/erpnext/issues/52236\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/frappe/erpnext/issues/52236\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">github.com/frappe/erpnext</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"github-row\">\n  <div class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"Issue\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\">\n\t  <svg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M7 2.3c3.14 0 5.7 2.56 5.7 5.7s-2.56 5.7-5.7 5.7A5.71 5.71 0 0 1 1.3 8c0-3.14 2.56-5.7 5.7-5.7zM7 1C3.14 1 0 4.14 0 8s3.14 7 7 7 7-3.14 7-7-3.14-7-7-7zm1 3H6v5h2V4zm0 6H6v2h2v-2z\"></path></svg>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"github-info-container\">\n    <h4>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/frappe/erpnext/issues/52236\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Tax-inclusive pricing: tax amount is wrong due to double rounding</a>\n    </h4>\n\n    <div class=\"github-info\">\n      <div class=\"date\">\n        opened <span class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2026-01-30\" data-time=\"17:38:23\" data-timezone=\"UTC\">05:38PM - 30 Jan 26 UTC</span>\n      </div>\n\n        <div class=\"date\">\n          closed <span class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2026-02-02\" data-time=\"07:12:35\" data-timezone=\"UTC\">07:12AM - 02 Feb 26 UTC</span>\n        </div>\n\n      <div class=\"user\">\n        <a href=\"https://github.com/mendozal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">\n          <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4621970?v=4\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">\n          mendozal\n        </a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"labels\">\n        <span style=\"display:inline-block;margin-top:2px;background-color: #B8B8B8;padding: 2px;border-radius: 4px;color: #fff;margin-left: 3px;\">\n          bug\n        </span>\n        <span style=\"display:inline-block;margin-top:2px;background-color: #B8B8B8;padding: 2px;border-radius: 4px;color: #fff;margin-left: 3px;\">\n          accounts\n        </span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n  <div class=\"github-row\">\n    <p class=\"github-body-container\">### Information about bug\n\nWhen using \"Is this Tax included in Basic Rate?\", the<span class=\"show-more-container\"><a href=\"\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"show-more\">…</a></span><span class=\"excerpt hidden\"> tax row amount can be wrong due to compound rounding. The grand total appears correct because adjust_grand_total_for_inclusive_tax() in the core silently corrects it, but the tax row and its GL entries remain incorrect.\n\nThis affects any tax rate and any item amount where the intermediate rounding of net_amount causes a loss of precision. It's easier to trigger with low-precision settings but can happen at any precision level where rounding crosses a boundary.\n\nThe effective precision comes from the currency's decimal places or the global \"Currency Precision\" in System Settings (whichever applies). Both paths lead to the same situation.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n- Set currency precision to 0 (either via currency settings or System Settings &gt; Currency Precision)\n- Create a Sales Taxes and Charges Template: 10%, \"Is this Tax included in Basic Rate?\" checked\n- Create a Sales Invoice, one item, rate = 50,000\n- Submit\n\nCalculation:\n\n- net_amount = round(50,000 / 1.10) = round(45,454.545...) = 45,455 (commercial rounding)\n- Expected tax: 50,000 − 45,455 = 4,545\n- Actual tax (what ERPNext computes): round(0.10 × 45,455) = round(4,545.5) = 4,546\n- Grand total shows 50,000 (correct, silently fixed by adjust_grand_total_for_inclusive_tax()), but the tax row shows 4,546 instead of 4,545. The tax account GL entry is therefore wrong by 1.\n- Row shows total of 50,001\n\nRoot cause:\n\n`erpnext/controllers/taxes_and_totals.py around line 581:`\n\n`current_tax_amount = (tax_rate / 100.0) * item.net_amount`\n\n`net_amount` is already rounded. Multiplying it back by the rate introduces a second rounding pass. The correct calculation:\n\n\ncurrent_tax_amount = item.amount - item.net_amount\nThis gives the exact tax without double rounding.\n\nHappens regardless of rounding method (Banker's, Commercial).\n\n### Module\n\naccounts\n\n### Version\n\nFrappe version: 16.4.1\nERPNext version: 16.3.0\n\n### Installation method\n\ndocker\n\n### Relevant log output / Stack trace / Full Error Message.\n\n```shell\n\n```</span></p>\n  </div>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>But it was closed because apparently is working as expected (last image in the issue).</p>\n<p>But I’m still seeing this issue on my end. Basically the tax is increased by 1 due to double rounding somewhere.</p>\n<p>Please take a look at this image. the total in the sales tax template is 50,001 instead of 50,000.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/c/5/c5e41684bfb032a45b5c0581465e106112272bfd.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/c5e41684bfb032a45b5c0581465e106112272bfd\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/c/5/c5e41684bfb032a45b5c0581465e106112272bfd_2_449x499.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"seCJKqNUnRJot0C4S7de4vra51H\" width=\"449\" height=\"499\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/c/5/c5e41684bfb032a45b5c0581465e106112272bfd_2_449x499.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/c/5/c5e41684bfb032a45b5c0581465e106112272bfd_2_673x748.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/c/5/c5e41684bfb032a45b5c0581465e106112272bfd_2_898x998.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"242424\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1508×1676 228 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/9/8/98818973403b5ab31971a6f65843a6ff5aabc756.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/98818973403b5ab31971a6f65843a6ff5aabc756\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/98818973403b5ab31971a6f65843a6ff5aabc756_2_690x338.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"lL86DznJ5PoXEl72jYNc5AfpXam\" width=\"690\" height=\"338\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/98818973403b5ab31971a6f65843a6ff5aabc756_2_690x338.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/98818973403b5ab31971a6f65843a6ff5aabc756_2_1035x507.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/9/8/98818973403b5ab31971a6f65843a6ff5aabc756_2_1380x676.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"242424\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1530×750 55.2 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>I tried different approaches, moving from banker’s rounding to commercial rounding. Using 0 precision in the currency precision field. Nothing changes this result.</p>\n<p>I can’t reopen the issue, and before opening another one. Is anyone having this issue or is able to replicate it?</p>\n<p>This is a clean install with US region and USD currency. The tax template “US ST 6%” was modified to have 10% tax rate and “<strong>Is this Tax included in Basic Rate?</strong>” is checked for tax inclusive pricing.</p>\n<p>The issue even happens to me with 2 decimal places</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/a/0/a0f272a1726905a6bab2f5bc76795f341264a62b.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/a0f272a1726905a6bab2f5bc76795f341264a62b\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/a/0/a0f272a1726905a6bab2f5bc76795f341264a62b_2_490x500.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"mXNPUkQcQaKjZtdQLwDng8pkZbt\" width=\"490\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/a/0/a0f272a1726905a6bab2f5bc76795f341264a62b_2_490x500.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/a/0/a0f272a1726905a6bab2f5bc76795f341264a62b_2_735x750.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/a/0/a0f272a1726905a6bab2f5bc76795f341264a62b_2_980x1000.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"232323\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1504×1534 202 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
