      "created_at": "2026-02-04T12:01:04.045Z",
      "cooked": "<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/mendozal\">@mendozal</a></p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mendozal\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"160161\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/mendozal/48/93136_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> mendozal:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The issue even happens to me with 2 decimal places</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I tried it on my site and I got the same result as your 2 decimal picture which is I think to me perfectly fine<br>\n45,454.55 X 1.1 = 50,000.01 (after rounding up)<br>\nIs your issue that a client will have a problem with $0.01 in tax?<br>\nIf so then I think you can set the default rounding off account to the tax account so that it becomes super accurate.<br>\nHave I understood your problem properly?</p>",
